    "user_request_original": "Design a 22-layer dielectric bandpass filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-band IR transmission. Stack topology: CaF2 | (Ge/ZnS)_4 | Ge_cavity | (Ge/ZnS)_3 | Ge_cavity | (Ge/ZnS)_4 | Air. Initialize all Ge layers at quarter-wave thickness for 4.45μm center wavelength (n_Ge≈4.0, thickness≈278nm). Initialize all ZnS layers at quarter-wave thickness (n_ZnS≈2.3, thickness≈484nm). Initialize both cavity spacers at half-wave thickness (≈556nm). Set thickness search bounds: Ge layers [150, 450]nm, ZnS layers [300, 650]nm, cavity spacers [400, 750]nm. Verify material registry accepts 'Ge' and 'ZnS' as valid identifiers before optimization. Optimize all 22 layer thicknesses to maximize transmittance in 4.15-4.35μm and 4.55-4.75μm bands while minimizing transmittance in 3.60-4.00μm and 4.85-5.20μm bands. Use coherent TMM at normal incidence. Log initialization thickness vector and material lookup results for diagnostic purposes. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 22 layer thicknesses of an alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric stack with two central Ge cavities on a CaF2 substrate. Maximize average transmittance in 4150–4350 nm and 4550–4750 nm bands while minimizing average transmittance in 3600–4000 nm and 4850–5200 nm bands under normal-incidence plane wave illumination using coherent TMM.",
